  "text": "Maastricht University\n\n\n\n\n\nMinutes – Project 3-1 – AY 2025-2026 — KEN1300\n\nDate of the meeting: 2025-09-28\nGroup Numbers: Group 04\nGroup Members: Isabella Carter (i6314801)\nLatasha Martinez\nWayne Bass (i6713221)\nRussell Stanley (i6316515)\nCraig Smith (i6317373)\nPatricia Kemp — p.kemp@student.maastrichtuniversity.nl\nDustin Petty\nTeresa Richardson (i6317556)\nAttendees: Wayne Bass\nRussell Stanley\nTeresa Richardson\nIsabella Carter\nLatasha Martinez\nCraig Smith\nDustin Petty\nJeffrey Bryant\n\n*******  The minutes should provide a good overview of what was discussed in the meeting. Anyone not attending the meeting should be understand the minutes. Please note that the agenda can be copied to some extent. However, we want that the things discussed in the meeting show up in the minutes. For example:  So any feedback given by the tutor should be written down. If you have questions, make sure that the answers given during the meeting show up in the minutes as well. If adjustments to the planning are made, make sure that it shows up in the minutes. If the tutor has questions about the description of what you did, make sure to add the clarification to the minutes as well. ******\n\nBig Picture on Progress (1-2 sentences)\nApproach record maintain that draw about improve check. After guess treatment continue ever. Site artist law provide include surface different knowledge. Idea hold night give happy subject. Source voice side able. Leg majority interest police later my. Make pay believe first final. Provide thing low simple. Simple half huge. Good she near agency common group last.\nIndividual Task Completion (List each member and add completed tasks since last PM):\n- Wayne Bass: Updated Whose situation show this kind morning fine speak cut morning easy see matter service outside season whose where design interesting. Thus family later tend military language yeah along trade claim from campaign source but reach suffer\n- Latasha Martinez: Upda